# One line-ending convention for every text file: LF, both in the repo and
# in the working tree. This checkout lives on a Windows mount where editors
# default to CRLF, which otherwise shows every tracked file as modified and
# turns any commit into a whole-file diff (git stored the CRLF bytes
# verbatim, since nothing normalized them on the way in).
# `text=auto` only applies to files git detects as text; binaries are
# additionally declared below so they are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary types -- never normalize these, even if a heuristic ever
# misdetects them as text.
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
